1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,408
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 20.

2
00:00:05,028 --> 00:00:09,266
The menu repeats until every valid item has been chosen at least once.

3
00:00:09,266 --> 00:00:13,064
Each choice sets done one, done two or done three to true.

4
00:00:13,064 --> 00:00:16,586
Which do while condition ends the loop at the right time?

5
00:00:18,287 --> 00:00:21,236
Try a run. Enter two: done two becomes true.

6
00:00:21,236 --> 00:00:23,376
Not everything is done, so repeat.

7
00:00:23,996 --> 00:00:28,137
Enter one, then two again: done one is true, and done two stays true.

8
00:00:28,137 --> 00:00:30,396
done three is still false, so repeat.

9
00:00:31,016 --> 00:00:34,285
Enter three: now all three are true, so the loop must stop.

10
00:00:35,885 --> 00:00:38,894
So the loop continues while not everything is done.

11
00:00:38,894 --> 00:00:41,799
All done is done one and done two and done three.

12
00:00:41,799 --> 00:00:44,341
Negate it: not, of that whole and.

13
00:00:44,341 --> 00:00:47,039
By De Morgan's law, that is the same as not done

14
00:00:47,039 --> 00:00:49,892
one, or not done two, or not done three.

15
00:00:51,492 --> 00:00:55,079
So the condition is not, of done one and done two and done three.

16
00:00:55,899 --> 00:00:59,899
Confusing all done, with and, with any done, with or, when you negate.

17
00:01:00,619 --> 00:01:03,552
Exam tip: write the stopping condition first, in

18
00:01:03,552 --> 00:01:06,694
words, then put a not around it for the do while.

19
00:01:06,694 --> 00:01:08,736
Check the result with De Morgan.
